\cb3         category: \cf9 \strokec9 "Tech & Coding"\cf0 \strokec5 ,\cb1 \
\cb3         author: \cf9 \strokec9 "Krishna Raninga"\cf0 \strokec5 ,\cb1 \
\cb3         date: \cf9 \strokec9 "September 25, 2026"\cf0 \strokec5 ,\cb1 \
\cb3         readTime: \cf10 \strokec10 3\cf0 \strokec5 ,\cb1 \
\cb3         likes: \cf10 \strokec10 24\cf0 \strokec5 ,\cb1 \
\cb3         liked: \cf8 \strokec8 false\cf0 \strokec5 ,\cb1 \
\cb3         image: \cf9 \strokec9 "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1555066931-4365d14bab8c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=80"\cf0 \strokec5 ,\cb1 \
\cb3         content: \cf9 \strokec9 `In modern web development, many developers jump straight into hefty frameworks like React, Next.js, or Vue without truly mastering the foundation. However, building interactive applications using pure HTML5, CSS3, and JavaScript teaches you how the DOM truly works.\\n\\nFrom handling event listeners, parsing localStorage, manipulating layout engines, to handling file readers for image uploads directly on the client side\'97vanilla JavaScript gives you complete command over the browser. This project is a testament that responsive and smooth interactive web applications do not strictly require heavy node runtimes or complex setups.`\cf0 \strokec5 ,\cb1 \
